A:

As the response's data object is static in that scenario:
export default connect((state) => 
  {
    return ({
      response: state.apiResponse
    }) 

})(MyComponent); 

You can also pass null response object in connect if you want to use undefined and not trigger this error.
export default connect( (
  )=> 
    { // ...
      return <MyComponent  response={undefined}/> // or pass null or false too!
    }
)

A common mistake while writing reactjs apps.
